From d3da15a55e4477f9f2f095daa054f38829d2d631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:14:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a chat's verified relay of the user's reply
 counts as human progress for the no-progress budget [daveey]

kanban-d1b921f32e: t_01a1cc1a8bb39958 was stopped for 5 no-progress runs although David
answered every needs_input ask; each answer reached the card as an agent comment from his chat.

- kanban_comment relays_user_message=true: verified (interactive chat, not a worker/child; a user
  message newer than the card's latest ask; one relay per message per card) and recorded as
  relayed_human {session, message_id, at} on the commented event; writer_kind stays agent.
- dashboard POST /comments accepts relayed_human from the cross_task courier beside
  writer_kind=agent and stores it as sent (via=remote).
- kanban_no_progress.progress_marker counts commented events carrying relayed_human.
- detection: an escalation right after a chat unblocked a needs_input block with no marked relay
  logs no_progress_relay_suspect (event + owner-card note).
